# scripts/sites.verified: FILE TAB FUNCTION TAB VERDICT TAB REASON. A catalog or relcache call that SQL can reach and whose result is not tested (scripts/check-sites.py), read: guarded (the reason says where the OID is checked or held), fixed (a regress case in surface_null_args), unreachable (why no dropped or invalid OID gets there).
src/agg/approx.c	sift_approx_trans	guarded	the type is get_fn_expr_argtype of the call: a type the parser resolved; the function tests the hash function of the entry (OidIsValid) and raises when it has none
src/agg/flat/keypush.c	join_equality	guarded	the type is the vartype of a Var of the statement being planned, which the parser resolved; lookup_type_cache raises for an unknown type, it never returns NULL
src/agg/refuse.c	tables_have_sift_index	guarded	the OID is the relid of an RTE of the statement being planned or executed: the parser locked the relation, so it cannot be dropped before the statement ends
src/agg/scope_unread.c	sift_agg_scope_unread	guarded	the OID is the relid of an RTE of the statement being planned or executed: the parser locked the relation, so it cannot be dropped before the statement ends
